From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:36:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 6 part 1: plans and usage limits, invoices and
 payments, custom domains

- Security fix: client admins could change their own organization's plan,
  status or parent agency through the API. Those columns are now locked;
  changes go through govern_organization (platform staff or the parent
  agency's admins only).
- Plans with per-metric limits, usage metering and limit enforcement in the
  database (texts, emails, AI requests, outreach, contacts, team, websites).
  Agencies define plans, assign them to clients, suspend or reactivate them.
- Invoices and estimates with deposits, tax and database-computed totals;
  customer page with card payment via the business's own Stripe account
  (Checkout, signed per-account webhooks, refunds), estimate accept/decline,
  convert to invoice, manual cash/check payments.
- Custom domains for hosted sites, verified by DNS TXT record; middleware
  serves only verified domains and falls through for unknown hosts.
- Branding for customer pages, full data export (works while suspended),
  Invoices and Plan & account screens, invoice and usage AI tools.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
